      "step_description": "Connect the proposed mechanism to replicated empirical evidence to confirm the causal link between action-belief contradiction and dissonant discomfort. Cite Festinger and Carlsmith’s 1959 landmark forced compliance study: participants who completed a tedious, boring task and were paid only $1 to lie to a fellow participant that the task was enjoyable reported significantly higher discomfort (and later adjusted their belief about the task’s enjoyability to reduce dissonance) than participants paid $20, who had sufficient external justification for the counter-attitudinal lie and thus experienced minimal dissonant arousal."
    },
