      "action": "Map candidate scenarios to established market failure categories",
      "description": "Cross-reference each candidate against the universally accepted classes of market failure to narrow valid options: 1) Externalities (positive/negative production/consumption spillovers), 2) Pure public goods (non-excludable, non-rivalrous goods underprovided by the market), 3) Imperfect market power (monopoly/oligopoly restricting output to raise prices above marginal cost), 4) Information asymmetry (adverse selection, moral hazard), 5) Merit goods (underconsumed socially beneficial goods e.g., routine vaccines) / demerit goods (overconsumed socially harmful goods e.g., unregulated tobacco sales), 6) Factor immobility (persistent misallocation of labor/capital due to geographic/occupational barriers)."
