  "core_definition_of_continuity_at_a_point": "A function f(x) is continuous at x = c if and only if three mutually dependent conditions are satisfied: 1) f(c) is defined and finite, 2) the two-sided limit limₓ→c f(x) exists and is finite, 3) limₓ→c f(x) = f(c).",
