      "Step 4: Relate the bound to the ε threshold: To get |f(x) - 3| < ε, substitute the neighborhood bound to get |x - 2| * 16 < ε, so |x - 2| < ε/16.",
      "Step 5: Define the valid δ: Choose δ = min(1, ε/16), which satisfies both the initial neighborhood restriction and the ε-dependent bound.",
      "Step 6: Verify the δ works: For any ε > 0, if |x - 2| < δ, then |x - 2| < 1 (so |x + 1|² < 16) and |x - 2| < ε/16, so |f(x) - 3| < (ε/16) * 16 = ε. This formally confirms limₓ→2 f(x) = f(2)."
