  "Question": "When solving the time-independent non-relativistic Schrödinger equation for an isolated, unperturbed hydrogen atom (assume an infinitely heavy proton, no external fields, no spin-dependent interactions, and no quantum electrodynamic corrections), four graduate students proposed the following claims about the resulting energy eigenvalues and their properties. Which claim is ACCURATE?",
  "Options": {
