    "B": "If we replace the Coulomb potential V(r) = -e²/(4πε₀r) with a generic central potential V(r) ∝ rᵏ where k ≠ -1, the energy eigenvalues will still depend only on the principal quantum number n, not on the orbital angular momentum quantum number l.",
