            "misconception": "The higher the transaction isolation level, the better the system performance",
            "correction": "Higher isolation levels require stricter concurrency control (e.g., more locks, longer lock holding time), which reduces system throughput and increases latency. For read-heavy, consistency-tolerant scenarios (e.g., social media feeds), Read Committed is often a better choice than Serializable."
        },
        {
            "misconception": "MVCC completely eliminates locks and has no concurrency conflicts",
            "correction": "MVCC only eliminates read-write locks by maintaining multiple data versions, but write-write conflicts still require locks for coordination. In addition, MVCC brings additional overhead of version chain management and garbage collection of old versions."
