        {
            "misconception": "Serializable isolation level means transactions are executed serially without interleaving",
            "correction": "Serializable isolation only requires that the execution result of concurrent transactions is equivalent to some serial execution order. Transactions can still be interleaved during actual execution as long as no concurrency anomalies occur, which ensures both consistency and certain throughput."
